    {
      "id": "00000000-0000-4000-8288-000000000021",
      "name": "Start Here",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -40,
        -460
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "content": "# START HERE: XB Ops Alert Email (shared sub-workflow)\n\n- **When:** another n8n workflow calls it with Execute Workflow (AC2 stock alerts first; EnergyGrid and the member-sync daily summary later). It has no webhook and no schedule.\n- **Input (closed):** `system` (AC2-STOCK, ENERGYGRID, MEMBER-SYNC), `severity` (ERROR, WARN, INFO), `key`, `short`, `lines[]`. Anything else is refused with a fixed reason code and no email.\n- **Flow:** validate -> read the recent rows of the Data Table `xb_alert_email_log` -> fold or flood decision -> one Gmail send -> one log row -> return `{ ok, outcome, code }`.\n- **Subject:** `[XB alert] <SYSTEM> <SEVERITY> <short>`. Plain-text body from the allowlisted fields only.\n- **Fold:** the same system:key within 60 min of its last sent email is logged `folded`; the next real send says `(+k folded since HH:MM)` (SGT).\n- **Flood, per system:** after 10 alert emails of one system in 60 min, that system's further alerts are logged `folded_flood` and one `[XB alert] <SYSTEM> WARN alert_flood` email goes out per 60 min for it. Other systems are not affected.\n- **One system per email:** every email names exactly one system; a request that names another system is refused.\n- **Failures:** Gmail has no retry (a retry can double-send). A failed send is logged `send_failed` with a code and returned, never thrown. A failed log write never blocks the answer.\n- Do not add HTTP Request, Execute Command, file, database or AI nodes.",
        "height": 420,
        "width": 900
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "00000000-0000-4000-8288-000000000022",
      "name": "Setup",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        900,
        -460
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "content": "# Setup (local import copy only)\n\n- Import inactive. Publishing it so callers can run it is a separate owner OK.\n\n## Required manual configuration:\n\n- **Send Alert Email**\n  - `To`: replace `REPLACE_WITH_OPERATIONS_INBOX` with the operations inbox, in the local import copy only.\n- **Read Recent Log**, **Log Held Back Alert**, **Log Email Sent**, **Log Send Failed**\n  - `Data table`: replace `REPLACE_WITH_ALERT_LOG_TABLE_ID` with the ID of `xb_alert_email_log`.\n\nThe Gmail credential is bound in n8n only. Fold window and flood cap: `FOLD_MINUTES` and `FLOOD_CAP` in **Decide Fold Or Send**.",
        "height": 420,
        "width": 620
      }
    }
  ],
